    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The Celtiberians were a group of Celtic-speaking peoples, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arevaci">Arevaci</a> and Belli, living in fortified towns on the plateau of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>.</li><li>Famed as warriors and sword-makers, they served as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenaries</a> and resisted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> in a series of wars from 181 to 133 BCE.</li><li>The fall of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/numantia">Numantia</a> in 133 BCE broke their independence, and after the Sertorian War they were absorbed into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispania">Roman Spain</a>.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The poet <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/catullus">Catullus</a> mocked a Celtiberian named Egnatius for brushing his teeth with urine, a custom that the historian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/diodorus-siculus">Diodorus Siculus</a> also reported among the Celtiberians.</p></aside>
    </section>

